  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 17 May 1967; twelve Unionist candidates nominated for twelve seats, no contest (Mid-Ulster Mail, 6 May 1967, p. 1). 'There is to be no contest for the twelve seats on Cookstown Urban Council. Only twelve candidates handed in their nomination papers at the Town Hall on Wednesday and all are Unionists.' New members: Espey Donaldson and Archibald Macrory; Norman Clements and Robert Vaughan retired. Returned unopposed."
